==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: F_AuthRequired is the sole fact that forbids a successful Operation from having no presented token. Removing it lets Alloy invent an Operation that succeeds with no auth, which the injection forces to exist; both auth predicates then find that counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_TokenBinding  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_TokenBinding.als
    rationale: F_TokenBinding is the only fact pinning caller to presentedToken.owner. With it removed, the injection forces an Operation whose caller is someone other than the token owner, violating FR-002's payload-vs-context rule.
    expected to FAIL: FR_002_IdentityFromAuth
      - FR_002_IdentityFromAuth: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: F_ClosedTaskEditRule is the sole encoder of the 409 task_closed contract. Removing it lets Alloy find a successful EditOp on a Done task whose request neither reopens it nor changes status — the injection forces exactly that shape.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLog.als
    rationale: F_DeletionLog is the sole link between successful DeleteOps and TaskDeletion log entries. Removing it lets Alloy invent a successful delete with no corresponding log row; the injection forces that orphaned delete.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionAttribution  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionAttribution.als
    rationale: F_DeletionAttribution is the sole fact tying td.deleter to the recording op's caller. Removing it allows misattribution; the injection forces a log entry whose recorded deleter differs from the actual operation caller.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_018_DeletionLog
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLog: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogAppendOnly  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogAppendOnly.als
    rationale: F_DeletionLogAppendOnly is the only fact that forbids two distinct TaskDeletion rows for the same delete event (duplicate / overwrite). The injection forces two log entries sharing a single source operation, which append-only must rule out.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_FlatPermissions  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_FlatPermissions.als
    rationale: F_FlatPermissions is the only fact stating that outcome is invariant under caller identity (given same kind/target/args). Removing it lets two authenticated callers with identical requests reach different outcomes; the injection forces that role-discrimination shape.
    expected to FAIL: FR_004_FlatPermissions
      - FR_004_FlatPermissions: FAIL (expected)

